//! OASIS MQTT Version 3.1.1 §2.2: the fixed header is a four-bit control packet
//! type, a DUP flag, a two-bit QoS level and a RETAIN flag, followed by the
//! Remaining Length — a variable-length integer of one to four octets, seven bits
//! each with a continuation bit (§2.2.3). MQTT Version 5.0 §2.1.1 keeps the same
//! fixed header. The length is not at a fixed width, so it is decoded into the
//! item list rather than placed in the field table.
//!
//! Generated by dev/protogen from dev/protogen/specs/mqtt.toml. Field layouts
//! come from the RFC cited above; edit the spec, not this file.

use crate::field::FieldDesc;
use crate::proto::{ProtoDesc, ProtoId};

